              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/AUTOMATH"} AUTOMATH
          %p
            %a{:href => "http://uf-ias-2012.wikispaces.com/file/view/deB1.pdf/401388596/deB1.pdf"} On the roles of types in mathematics
          %p
            The notion of judgmental or definitional equality was later introduced by
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Per+Martin-L%C3%B6f"} Per Martin-Löf
            %a{:href => "http://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0049237X09703659"} Hauptsatz for Intuitionistic Simple Type Theory
            and generalized in Type Theory. He discusses this notion in the paper
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "http://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0049237X08707274"} About Models for Intuitionistic Type Theory and The notion of Definitional Equality
          %p The extension from AUTOMATH is that one adds the notion of data type (natural number), of constructors (zero and successor) and primitive recursion as definitional equality. The motivation is that one can consider the schema of primitive recursion as a definition of a function.
          %p This was also influenced by natural deduction, where constructors correspond to introduction rules and the work of Gödel on system T.
          %p
            With this extension, one obtains a programming language with dependent types and where computations correspond to unfolding of definitions (that can be primitive recursive definitions). This programming language has the feature that all computations terminate. This has been also considered in functional programming, see e.g. the discussion in
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "http://uf-ias-2012.wikispaces.com/file/view/turner.pdf/401400700/turner.pdf"} this paper
          %p
            A description of the evaluation algorithm using techniques from functional programming can be found in
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "http://uf-ias-2012.wikispaces.com/file/view/strong-reduction.pdf/402005168/strong-reduction.pdf"} this work of Gregoire and Leroy
          %h2#see_also See also
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equality"}> equality
                ,
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equality+in+type+theory"} equality in type theory
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/propositional+equality"}> propositional equality
                ,
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/typal+equality"} typal equality
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coercion"} coercion
          %h2#references References
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                Robin Adams,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Pure type systems with judgemental equality
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://dl.acm.org/citation.cfm?id=1114675"} web
            %li
              %p
                Vincent Siles, Hugo Herbelin,
                %em Equality is typable in semi-full pure type systems
                (
                %a{:href => "http://pauillac.inria.fr/~herbelin/publis/lics-SilHer10-pts-typed-conv.pdf"}> pdf
                )
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Egbert+Rijke"}> Egbert Rijke
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Introduction+to+Homotopy+Type+Theory"} Introduction to Homotopy Type Theory
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/martinescardo/HoTTEST-Summer-School/main/HoTT/hott-intro.pdf"} pdf
          %p The first paper to mention intensional equality (and the fact that it should be decidable) may be:
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kurt+G%C3%B6del"}> Kurt Gödel
              ,
              = succeed "." do
                %em Über eine bisher noch nicht benützte Erweiterung des finiten Standpunktes
          %p The distinction between definitional equality and “book” equality:
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Nicolaas+de+Bruijn"}> Nicolaas de Bruijn
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Automath"} Automath
          %p
            The notion of definitional equality in the context of (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dependent+type+theory"}> dependent
            )
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type+theory"} type theory
          %ul
            %li#Thompson91
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Simon+Thompson"}> Simon Thompson
              , §5.2.1 in:
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Type+Theory+and+Functional+Programming"} Type Theory and Functional Programming
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "http://www.cs.kent.ac.uk/people/staff/sjt/TTFP"} webpage
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "http://www.cs.kent.ac.uk/people/staff/sjt/TTFP/ttfp.pdf"} pdf
          %p
            specifically in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Coq"} Coq
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/proof+assistant"} proof assistant
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Adam+Chlipala"}> Adam Chlipala
              , §10.1 in:
              = succeed "," do
                %em Certified programming with dependent types
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "https://mitpress.mit.edu/books/certified-programming-dependent-types"} ISBN:9780262026659
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "http://adam.chlipala.net/cpdt/cpdt.pdf"} pdf
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "http://adam.chlipala.net/cpdt/"} book webpage
